  basic/solution/basic.p4
  p4runtime/{topology.json,mycontroller.py,advanced_tunnel.p4}
  p4runtime/build/{advanced_tunnel.json,advanced_tunnel.p4.p4info.txtpb}
  ecn/{topology.json,s1-runtime.json,s2-runtime.json,s3-runtime.json}
  mri/{topology.json,s1-runtime.json,s2-runtime.json,s3-runtime.json}
  firewall/pod-topo/{topology,s1-runtime,s2-runtime,s3-runtime,s4-runtime}.json   (2026-09-18)
  firewall/basic.p4                                                              (2026-09-18)
  calc/{topology.json,s1-runtime.json,calc.p4}                                   (2026-09-18)

COMPILED HERE, NOT COPIED (2026-09-18; the allow list is
test_convert.GENERATED_FIXTURES, and every name in it is checked to exist so the exemption
cannot rot into a silent pass):

  firewall/build/{basic.json,basic.p4.p4info.txtpb}
  firewall/build/{firewall.json,firewall.p4.p4info.txtpb}
  calc/build/{calc.json,calc.p4.p4info.txtpb}

  Neither exercise has ever been built in this checkout -- there is no build/ under either --
  and TICKET-P2's G4 means a package names the program each switch runs, so a package that
  does not carry those artefacts cannot be converted at all. Produced with:

    p4c-bm2-ss --p4v 16 --p4runtime-files build/<stem>.p4.p4info.txtpb \
               -o build/<stem>.json ~/tutorials/exercises/<exercise>/<stem>.p4

  p4c-bm2-ss 1.2.5.15 (SHA 5b948b037a BUILD: Release), /usr/local/bin/p4c-bm2-ss.
  Their bmv2 json therefore carries `program: /home/adam/tutorials/exercises/<ex>/<stem>.p4`,
  which is where the source really is. That absolute path is also why a bmv2 json's sha256 is
  NOT a stable identifier for "this program" (measured in TICKET-P1 B: the same .p4 compiled
  in two directories gave two shas); the p4info's sha256 is stable and is the one pre-flight
  prints and the tests compare.

WHY firewall AND calc. firewall/pod-topo is the ONLY shipped exercise whose topology.json uses
tutorials' per-switch `program` override -- s1 runs build/firewall.json, s2-s4 fall through to
the Makefile's `DEFAULT_PROG = basic.p4` -- so it is the only fixture that can tell a converter
which reads that field from one which drops it. Its runtime files pair with it: s1-runtime.json
names firewall's p4info inside the file and s2-s4's name basic's. calc is the single-switch,
two-host, zero-inter-switch-link shape, which `topo_from_json.switch_links` refused outright
until TICKET-P2.

